<title>GERMANY: Vereinsbank to shed 800 jobs in Germany.</title>
<headline>Vereinsbank to shed 800 jobs in Germany.</headline>
<dateline>MUNICH, Germany 1997-05-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Germany's Bayerische Vereinsbank AG said on Wednesday it plans to shed a net 800 jobs in Germany in the next one-and-a-half years.</p>
<p>Chief executive Albrecht Schmidt told the banks' annual shareholder meeting that Vereinsbank was subjecting itself to an efficiency test and planned to slim down its administrative staffing.</p>
<p>A spokesman for the bank said Vereinsbank had potential to shed 1,600 jobs through rationalisation and restructuring but that the bank planned to hire 800 sales staff.</p>
<p>Vereinsbank employed 21,825 people at the end of 1996 of whom about 20,000 were in Germany.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom, +49 69 756525</p>
